{"id":"mimid-1wgh.102","title":"JMAP: jmap-chat-did: a DID capability for ChatContact","description":"In scope by decision mimid-1wgh.98 (Mark, 2026-11-22). Not planned: read the draft, face the tension below, and put a plan in this field for Mark before any code.

WHAT THE DRAFT DOES. A capability signalling DID support, the DID methods a conforming server resolves and verifies, optional ChatContact DID binding, and DID-bound verification for a peer whose identity is a DID without a host.

READ IT AGAINST TODAY'S DECISION: mimid-1wgh.97 settled that a did:key may be an alsoKnownAs inside a did:webvh log and never a credential of its own, and mimid-1wgh.4.81.38 will read and show those entries. This draft is the natural JMAP home for that, and it reuses the supported-DID-method list from jmap-did. Check whether its method list and its verification rules can express 'did:webvh is authoritative, did:key is a second name' or whether they flatten the two, which would be a problem worth raising with Mark.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mark@reviewcommit.com","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.356232969Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","updated_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.356232969Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"mimid-1wgh.102","depends_on_id":"mimid-1wgh","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.386582889Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","metadata":"{}"}]}
